          ],
          "content": "Ganita Prakash | Grade 7"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.088,
            0.849,
            0.145
          ],
          "content": "order matters. She should wear socks and then shoes. If she wears shoes and then socks, Manasa will feel very uncomfortable and look very different."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.163,
            0.585,
            0.185
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "More Expressions and Their Terms"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.11,
            0.193,
            0.848,
            0.252
          ],
          "content": "？ **Example 7:** Amu, Charan, Madhu, and John went to a hotel and ordered four dosas. Each dosa cost ₹23, and they wish to thank the waiter by tipping ₹5. Write an expression describing the total cost."
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.383,
            0.255,
            0.616,
            0.273
          ],
          "content": "\\mathrm { C o s t \\; o f \\; 4 \\; d o s a s } = 4 \\times 2 3",
          "image_source": "images/page_8_equation_4.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.28,
            0.848,
            0.318
          ],
          "content": "Can the total amount with tip be written as $4 \\times 2 3 \\div 5 ?$ Evaluating it, we get"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.192,
            0.324,
            0.803,
            0.366
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_8_image_6.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.174,
            0.375,
            0.75,
            0.395
          ],
          "content": "Thus, $4 \\times 2 3 \\pm 5$ is a correct way of writing the expression."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.11,
            0.402,
            0.848,
            0.462
          ],
          "content": "? If the total number of friends goes up to 7 and the tip remains the same, how much will they have to pay? Write an expression for this situation and identify its terms."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.469,
            0.848,
            0.547
          ],
          "content": "? **Example 8:** Children in a class are playing “Fire in the mountain, run, run, run!”. Whenever the teacher calls out a number, students are supposed to arrange themselves in groups of that number. Whoever is not part of the announced group size, is out."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.551,
            0.362,
            0.661
          ],
          "content": "Ruby wanted to rest and sat on one side. The other 33 students were playing the game in the class."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.661,
            0.359,
            0.735
          ],
          "content": "The teacher called out ‘5’. Once children settled, Ruby wrote"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.385,
            0.552,
            0.903,
            0.741
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_8_image_12.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.734,
            0.239,
            0.751
          ],
          "content": "6 \\times 5 \\pm 3",
          "image_source": "images/page_8_equation_13.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.752,
            0.489,
            0.772
          ],
          "content": "(understood as 3 more than 6 × 5)"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.78,
            0.532,
            0.803
          ],
          "content": "Think and discuss why she wrote this."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.807,
            0.631,
            0.826
          ],
          "content": "The expression written as a sum of terms is—"
        },
        {
